# 32 random bytes that encrypt stored Obsidian credentials at rest AND derive
# the session-signing secret. Must be real key material — base64 (44 chars) or
# hex (64 chars); a passphrase is NOT accepted.
# Generate with: openssl rand -base64 32   (or: openssl rand -hex 32)
ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# DATA_DIR and BASE_URL are deliberately absent, and should stay that way.
#
# Railway seeds a service's suggested variables from this file, so anything
# listed here is offered to deployers as a production value. Both of these have
# a development-correct value that is actively harmful in production, and both
# have a working default already:
#
#   DATA_DIR  The Dockerfile sets it to /data, matching the volume mount. A
#             relative value like ./data resolves against the container's
#             WORKDIR instead, putting the vault and database on the ephemeral
#             layer where every redeploy discards them. Locally the code
#             defaults to ./data when unset.
#
#   BASE_URL  Derived from RAILWAY_PUBLIC_DOMAIN in production and from
#             http://localhost:3000 otherwise. Suggesting the localhost literal
#             pins a deployment's OAuth issuer to localhost, which breaks
#             sign-in with "Invalid origin".
#
# Set BASE_URL by hand only to pin a custom domain, and only as a complete
# origin including the scheme. See src/server/env.ts.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
